{
  "_format": {
    "description": "Pattern masking golden cases (docs/security.md 8.3). Apply `patterns` in order, each as a global regex replacement with the replacement string; `redacted` is true iff the output differs from the input. Regexes are valid for both Rust `regex` and java.util.regex. `cmd_preview_cases` use the same patterns with replacement '***' (docs/protocol.md 7 {cmd60}).",
    "replacement": "<redacted>",
    "cmd_preview_replacement": "***",
    "known_limitations": [
      "keyword_assignment consumes only the first token after ':' or '=' (so 'Authorization: Bearer <opaque>' would leave '<opaque>'); the earlier auth_header rule masks the value after the scheme first, and keyword_assignment then masks 'Authorization: Bearer' (hence '<redacted> <redacted>').",
      "long_token_40 also matches long path-like strings that consist only of [A-Za-z0-9+/_-] (over-masking is the safe direction).",
      "Patterns with a named group 'pre' and/or 'post' keep those groups and replace only the rest of the match (replacement = pre + replacement + post); patterns without them are replaced as a whole. Group names are the only extension of plain `regex.replace_all`; both Rust `regex` and java.util.regex accept `(?<name>...)`.",
      "credential_flag / mysql_password_flag / user_flag / env_secret favour over-masking for the flag and identifier forms they name; unrelated ordinary text must stay unchanged (see the negative cases)."
    ]
  },
  "patterns": [
    {
      "name": "auth_header",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>\\b(?:proxy-)?authorization[\"']?\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"']?(?:bearer|basic|token|digest|negotiate)\\s+)[^\\s\"']+"
    },
    {
      "name": "keyword_assignment",
      "regex": "(?i)(api[_-]?key|token|secret|password|passwd|authorization|bearer)\\s*[:=]\\s*\\S+"
    },
    {
      "name": "aws_access_key",
      "regex": "AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}"
    },
    {
      "name": "github_token",
      "regex": "gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}"
    },
    {
      "name": "sk_token",
      "regex": "sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}"
    },
    {
      "name": "vendor_token",
      "regex": "\\b(?:xox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}|npm_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}|github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}|glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}|AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{30,}|(?:sk|rk|pk)_(?:live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}|SG\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}|ya29\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,})"
    },
    {
      "name": "private_key_block",
      "regex": "-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----[\\s\\S]*?-----END [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----"
    },
    {
      "name": "jwt",
      "regex": "eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+"
    },
    {
      "name": "url_userinfo",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>\\b[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*://[^\\s/@:\"']+:)[^\\s/@\"']+(?<post>@)"
    },
    {
      "name": "credential_flag",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>\\B--?(?:password|passwd|pass|token|secret|api-?key|apikey|access-?token|auth-?token|client-?secret|oauth2-bearer)(?:\\s+|=))[^\\s\"'-][^\\s\"']*"
    },
    {
      "name": "user_flag",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>(?:\\B--(?:proxy-)?user|\\b(?:curl|wget)\\b[^\\n|;&]*?\\s-u)\\s+[^\\s:@\"']+:)[^\\s\"']*[^\\s\"'\\d][^\\s\"']*"
    },
    {
      "name": "mysql_password_flag",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>\\b(?:mysql(?:dump|admin|import|check|pump|show|slap)?|mariadb(?:-dump|-admin|-import|-check|-show)?)\\b[^\\n|;&]*?\\s(?-i:-p))[^\\s\"'-]\\S*"
    },
    {
      "name": "npm_auth",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>_auth(?:token|password)?\\s*[=\\s]\\s*)[^\\s\"']+"
    },
    {
      "name": "query_secret",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>[?&](?:key|token|api_?key|apikey|access_token|auth|sig|signature|secret|password|passwd|client_secret)=)[^&\\s\"'#]+"
    },
    {
      "name": "aws_secret",
      "regex": "(?i)(?<pre>\\baws[_-]?(?:secret[_-]?access[_-]?key|secret[_-]?key|session[_-]?token)[\"']?\\s*(?:=|:|\\s)\\s*[\"']?)[^\\s\"',;&]+"
    },
    {
      "name": "env_secret",
      "regex": "(?i)\\b[a-z0-9_.-]*(?:secret|passw(?:or)?d|token|credentials?|(?:api|private|access|auth|signing|encryption|ssh|master)[_-]?key|_key)[a-z0-9_.-]*[\"']?\\s*[=:]\\s*[\"']?[^\\s\"',;&]+"
    },
    {
      "name": "long_token_40",
      "regex": "[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]{40,}={0,2}"
    }
  ],
